CorrectionClass.description:
Certainty class of a correction of the program text.

# Examples

```
use nurt_contracts::report::CorrectionClass;

assert_eq!(CorrectionClass::Fuzzy.as_str(), "F");
```

Irreversible.description:
Reason why an effect is irreversible, reported in
[`Report::irreversible`].

# Examples

```
use nurt_contracts::report::Irreversible;

assert_eq!(Irreversible::RemoteRefUpdated.as_str(), "remote_ref_updated");
assert_eq!(
    "previous_content_not_kept".parse::<Irreversible>(),
    Ok(Irreversible::PreviousContentNotKept)
);
```

Record.description:
Record: a kind and fields in a fixed order.

This is the dynamic form used by `filter`, `select`, `sort` and other
stages that work on fields by name; the typed form of each kind is in
[`crate::record`] and converts to and from this form.

```
use nurt_contracts::value::{Record, RecordKind, Value};

let mut record = Record::new(RecordKind::Map).with("count", Value::Int(3));
record.set("label", Value::from("done"));
assert_eq!(record.field_names().collect::<Vec<_>>(), ["count", "label"]);
assert_eq!(record.get("count"), Some(&Value::Int(3)));
```

Regex.description:
Regular expression: pattern and flags.

The pattern is the source text of the expression without the enclosing
`/` and with `\/` already turned into `/`. The text form is
`/pattern/flags`.

```
use nurt_contracts::value::Regex;

let regex = Regex::new("a/b+", "i").unwrap();
assert_eq!(regex.to_string(), "/a\\/b+/i");
```

Range.description:
Inclusive range of integers: `5`, `1..5`, `40..`, `..9`, or every
integer.

Both bounds are inclusive; a missing bound is open. The start is never
greater than the end.

```
use nurt_contracts::value::Range;

let range = Range::new(Some(1), Some(5)).unwrap();
assert!(range.contains(5));
assert_eq!(range.to_string(), "1..5");
assert_eq!(Range::from_start(40).to_string(), "40..");
assert!(Range::new(Some(5), Some(1)).is_err());
```

Notable.description:
Code of an unusual effect reported in [`Report::notable`].

A notable effect is a description only; nothing is blocked because of
it. Thresholds are configurable under `report.notable.*`. Codes for which
[`Notable::computed_by_report`] is true are derived by the report builder
from the list of changes; all other codes are emitted by the command that
observed the condition.

# Examples

```
use nurt_contracts::report::{Notable, Severity};

assert_eq!(Notable::MassDelete.as_str(), "mass_delete");
assert_eq!(Notable::MassDelete.default_severity(), Severity::Warning);
assert!(Notable::MassDelete.computed_by_report());
assert!(Notable::NothingMatched.computed_by_report());
assert!(!Notable::Unchanged.computed_by_report());
```

Severity.description:
Importance of an unusual effect, in increasing order of importance.

# Examples

```
use nurt_contracts::report::Severity;

assert!(Severity::Alert > Severity::Warning);
assert_eq!(Severity::Notice.as_str(), "notice");
```

ErrorCode.description:
Stable error code of the language.

Codes are only added within a major version of the language;
the text form (`E_UNKNOWN_COMMAND`) is the JSON form.

At.description:
Position of an error: the execution stage and the place in the program
text.

Lines and columns start at 1; columns and lengths count Unicode scalar
values. Errors raised while a stage runs (for example `E_STALE` in stage
`5`) carry the stage without a place in the text.

```
use nurt_contracts::error::{At, Stage};

let at = At::new(2, 5, 3).with_stage(Stage::Bind);
assert_eq!(
    serde_json::to_value(at).unwrap(),
    serde_json::json!({"line": 2, "column": 5, "length": 3, "stage": "1"})
);
assert_eq!(At::stage(Stage::After).line, None);
```
